The order path runs from the chart's `postOrder` helper through the REST `OrderResource` into `OrderServiceImpl` and then the Hibernate DAO. I did not find a separate frontend component in the chart that calls these directly; the order-basket flow reaches `postOrder` through `postOrders`.

**Flow**

1. **Frontend request:** `postOrder` in `openmrs-esm-patient-chart` POSTs the order body to `${restBaseUrl}/order` via `openmrsFetch`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/orders/postOrders.ts:202-209}
2. **Batch caller:** `postOrders` walks the order basket items for a patient, builds each payload with the registered data-prep function, and calls `postOrder` for each one. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/orders/postOrders.ts:157-199}
3. **REST handler:** `OrderResource1_10.save` (the `/order` resource, inherited by `OrderResource1_8`, and by `OrderResource2_2`) calls `Context.getOrderService().saveOrder(delegate, null)`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-webservices.rest::omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_10/OrderResource1_10.java:323-329}
4. **Core service:** `OrderServiceImpl.saveOrder` delegates to the private `saveOrder(order, ctx, isRetrospective)`, which runs validation (existing-order check, date/concept/order-type defaults, previous-order checks, active-order overlap check) and then calls `saveOrderInternal`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core::api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/OrderServiceImpl.java:115-117}, @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core::api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/OrderServiceImpl.java:165-224}
5. **Persistence prep:** `saveOrderInternal` assigns an order number if missing, sets auto-expire rules for new orders, then calls `dao.saveOrder`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core::api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/OrderServiceImpl.java:350-379}
6. **Data access:** `HibernateOrderDAO.saveOrder` calls `HibernateUtil.saveOrUpdate` on the current Hibernate session, which is the database write. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core::api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/hibernate/HibernateOrderDAO.java:88-95}

The DAO interface declaration is `OrderDAO.saveOrder`, and the public service contract is `OrderService.saveOrder`. I did not read those two declarations, so their line ranges below are from grep hits, not from a read.

